    "kind": "analysis",
    "text": "# Investigation note: metric M385945, reporting month 2026-10-31\n\n**1. Executive finding**\nM385945 is in the **Amber (watch)** provisional band. Its provisional rate is **53.3%**, which is 8 of 15 denominator rows. That is down from 66.7% (Red) in September. The band is provisional and is not a client target. The metric still needs watching: 7 of 20 metric rows are Non_Compliant, up from 3, and 3 of those 7 were also non-compliant last month.\n\n**2. Current status and period (2026-10-31, observed)**\n- There are 20 metric rows, one per application, for 20 applications.\n- Compliant: 8. Non_Compliant: 7. Pending: 4. Not_Applicable: 1.\n- The denominator is 15, which is the Compliant plus Non_Compliant rows. Pending and Not_Applicable rows are left out, which matches the inferred EXCLUDES_PENDING scope.\n\n**3. Movement against 2026-09-30 (provisional)**\n- **Rate:** 6/9 (66.7%) to 8/15 (53.3%), a change of −13.3 percentage points. The band moved from Red to Amber.\n- **Main driver of the change:** the denominator grew from 9 to 15. In September, 5 rows were Not_Applicable (3 of them Exempt). In October only 1 was. So most of the rate change comes from which rows are counted, not just from changes in status.\n- **Non-compliant rows by application:**\n  - 2 are newly non-compliant: EON949297 (was Not_Applicable) and EON760352 (was Compliant).\n  - 3 stayed non-compliant: EON941302, EON856001 and EON787345.\n  - 2 have no September row: EON917742 and EON873875.\n  - All 3 applications that were non-compliant in September are still non-compliant, so none were resolved.\n- **Who reported:** 15 of October's 20 applications also reported in September, and 5 are new this month.\n\n**4. Main contributors (the 7 non-compliant rows)**\n- **Super division:** Super_Division_06 has 2. Super_Division_01, 02, 04, 05 and 08 have 1 each. Super_Division_03 has 0.\n- **Legal entity:** Legal_Entity_01 has 2 (EON949297 and EON941302). Legal_Entity_02, 15, 33 and 37 have 1 each.\n- No single unit stands out; the largest share in any one place is 2 of 7.\n**5. Testing and exception observations (observed)**\n- **Non-compliant rows:** 4 of the 7 had a completed test that failed. The recorded reasons are Test_Failed (2), Remediation_Overdue (1) and Open_Findings_Outstanding (1). The other 3 had no test, with reasons Test_Overdue (2) and No_Test_Performed (1).\n- **Failed tests overall:** 5 of 12 completed tests failed.\n- **Anomaly:** EON792667 is marked Compliant (Remediation_Verified) even though its test result is Fail.\n- **Pending rows:** 4 rows are waiting. Two are Awaiting_Test_Assignment and two are Test_In_Progress. They are outside the denominator, so how they resolve could change next month's rate.\n\n**6. Areas for further investigation (hypotheses, not validated)**\n- Find out why 3 Exempt or Not_Applicable rows from September are no longer Not_Applicable in October. Possible explanations are expired exemptions or a change in scope.\n- Look at the 3 applications that have been non-compliant for two months in a row (EON941302, EON856001, EON787345).\n- Check how a row can be Compliant with a failed test (EON792667).\n- Check whether the two Test_Overdue rows point to a gap in test scheduling.\n\n**7. Limitations**\n- **Possible conflict in the band's direction:** all 8 numerator rows are Compliant. The band treats a higher rate as worse, but that only fits if the numerator really stands for something unfavourable. Please confirm what the numerator means before relying on the band's direction.\n- **Small numbers:** with a denominator of 8 to 15, one row moves the rate by about 7 to 12 percentage points. Over the last 12 months the rate has swung between 25% and 78%.\n- **Provisional definitions:** the rate, the movement categories and the denominator scope (inferred from Pending rows) are all provisional.\n- **What the data doesn't have:** it holds no metric name or family, and the reasons in it don't establish causes, owners or remediation.",
